1
00:00:00,238 --> 00:00:03,190
Dolphins need air to breathe.

2
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:06,375
But they live in the ocean.

3
00:00:06,375 --> 00:00:08,750
So how do they sleep?

4
00:00:09,649 --> 00:00:13,100
You breathe on autopilot.

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:18,068
A dolphin chooses every breath.

6
00:00:18,068 --> 00:00:22,949
Fall fully asleep → stop breathing.

7
00:00:23,849 --> 00:00:27,094
Dolphins sleep with half the brain.

8
00:00:27,094 --> 00:00:30,404
The other half stays awake.

9
00:00:30,404 --> 00:00:35,349
Unihemispheric slow-wave sleep.

10
00:00:36,262 --> 00:00:39,449
The awake half stays on duty.

11
00:00:39,449 --> 00:00:43,831
A sleeping dolphin keeps one eye open.

12
00:00:43,831 --> 00:00:49,224
The eye on the opposite
side, watching for predators.

13
00:00:50,126 --> 00:00:52,969
They drift near the surface.

14
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:57,413
Rising every few minutes for a breath.

15
00:00:57,413 --> 00:01:01,625
Each half gets about 4 hours a day.

16
00:01:02,501 --> 00:01:05,232
New mothers get no luxury.

17
00:01:05,232 --> 00:01:09,363
For a whole month, mother
and baby barely sleep.

18
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:12,863
Half a brain asleep.

19
00:01:12,863 --> 00:01:15,882
One eye open.

20
00:01:15,882 --> 00:01:17,557
Still breathing.
